## Working boundaries

- {{few_project_specific_invariants_with_links_to_their_owners}}
- Reuse the owning module and public use case. Preserve state ownership and
  permitted dependencies; avoid duplicate implementations.
- Keep this task's user outcome and non-goals fixed unless explicitly changed.
  Resolve material conflicts with their owner; routine choices remain with the
  implementing agent.
- Use PACT for the document console and agreements, VERIFY for acceptance design
  and environment business verification, OPAID for implementation/unit tests/local
  checks, and CICD for authorized delivery and recovery when selected.
  Equivalent existing workflows: {{selected_workflow_sources_and_versions}}

## Verification and handoff

- Run {{applicable_real_check_commands}} for changed behavior and the final
  integrated candidate. Report actual results and omissions.
- Human walkthrough: {{normal_entry_inputs_expected_result_and_failures}}.
- Keep implementation, integration, runtime verification and human acceptance
  distinct. Do not invent approval or treat mocks as real-backend evidence.
- Parallel work shares effective sources and explicit write/interface ownership.
  Inspect and verify the integrated candidate before handoff.
- Use existing task/evidence records; do not create parallel status ledgers.
- Continue from effective agreements, stable scenarios, current candidate and
  environment evidence, then remaining work. Preserve historical results; an old
  pass does not automatically apply to a new candidate or environment.
- Separate intended behavior from observed facts. Changes to expected results
  need an authorized requirement change or justified test correction.
- Use the project's selected source/review/test/CI tools and this host's supported
  skill layout. Host-specific metadata does not change shared document meanings.
